/-
# Baer groups and Fitting groups (Kourovka Notebook Problem 2.21)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.21 (Sh. S. Kemkhadze): do the classes of
Baer and Fitting groups coincide?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import Mathlib.GroupTheory.IsSubnormal
public import WantedExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentThreeConjugatesFittingKourovka17Problem40Wanted

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.GroupTheory.BaerFittingGroupsKourovka2Problem21Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.21 (Sh. S.
Kemkhadze). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700097 (`KOU-2.21`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A Baer group is a group in which every cyclic subgroup is subnormal (Mathlib's
`Subgroup.IsSubnormal`); a Fitting group is generated by its normal nilpotent subgroups
(`fittingSubgroup G = ⊤`, `fittingSubgroup` of the Kourovka 17.40 entry, reused here). "The classes
coincide" is stated as an equivalence for every group in `Type`; every Fitting group is a Baer
group, so the content is the other direction.
-/

open MathlibExt.GroupTheory.NilpotentThreeConjugatesFittingKourovka17Problem40Wanted
  (fittingSubgroup)

/-- `G` is a Baer group: every cyclic subgroup of `G` is subnormal. -/
def IsBaerGroup (G : Type*) [Group G] : Prop :=
  ∀ g : G, (Subgroup.zpowers g).IsSubnormal

/-- `G` is a Fitting group: `G` is generated by its normal nilpotent subgroups, `F(G) = G`. -/
def IsFittingGroup (G : Type*) [Group G] : Prop :=
  fittingSubgroup G = ⊤

/-- Kourovka 2.21 (Sh. S. Kemkhadze): the classes of Baer groups and Fitting groups coincide. -/
def baerGroupsIffFittingGroups : Prop :=
  ∀ (G : Type) [Group G], IsBaerGroup G ↔ IsFittingGroup G

/--
Resolved false: the Kourovka Archive answers 2.21 "No", citing Dark; since every Fitting group is a
Baer group, this is a Baer group that is not a Fitting group. Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D.
Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue,
arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.21 (Sh. S. Kemkhadze); resolution:
R. S. Dark, A prime Baer group, Math. Z. 105 (1968), 294-298, Kourovka Archive, Problem 2.21: No,
https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v49.
-/
public theorem_wanted baerGroupsIffFittingGroups_refuted : ¬ baerGroupsIffFittingGroups

end MathlibExt.GroupTheory.BaerFittingGroupsKourovka2Problem21Wanted
